 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
 
+## Board Publication
+
+A published board can be viewed by anyone who has its secret public URL, without signing in. The URL is returned as `public_url` in the board JSON, and is `null` while the board is not published.
+
+Only account admins can publish or unpublish a board.
+
+Public pages are read-only and show the board's columns and published cards. Each column and card also has its own page, at `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:column_id` and `/:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`. Drafted cards, and cards from other boards, are never shown.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes a board. Publishing a board that is already published keeps its existing public URL.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the board, in the same shape as `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id` (abridged below), where `public_url` is set:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcm",
+  "name": "Fizzy",
+  "all_access": false,
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.534Z",
+  "auto_postpone_period_in_days": 30,
+  "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/boards/03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcm",
+  "public_url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/public/boards/Qm3xv8PkYwLr2TnbZ6sUeA9C"
+}
+```
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes a board. Its public URL stops working. Publishing the board again creates a new public URL.
+
+__Response:__
+
+Returns `204 No Content` on success.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
diff --git a/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c3b611c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class Boards::PublicationsControllerTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
+  setup do
+    sign_in_as :kevin
+    @board = boards(:writebook)
+  end
+
+  test "publish" do
+    assert_difference -> { Board::Publication.count }, +1 do
+      post board_publication_path(@board)
+    end
+
+    assert_redirected_to edit_board_path(@board)
+    assert @board.reload.published?
+  end
+
+  test "publish as JSON exposes the public URL" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+
+    assert_response :created
+    assert_equal public_board_url(@board.reload.publication), @response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+  end
+
+  test "publishing an already published board keeps the same key" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board)
+    key = @board.reload.publication.key
+
+    assert_no_difference -> { Board::Publication.count } do
+      post board_publication_path(@board)
+    end
+
+    assert_equal key, @board.reload.publication.key
+  end
+
+  test "unpublish" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board)
+
+    assert_difference -> { Board::Publication.count }, -1 do
+      delete board_publication_path(@board)
+    end
+
+    assert_redirected_to edit_board_path(@board)
+    assert_not @board.reload.published?
+  end
+
+  test "unpublish as JSON" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board)
+
+    delete board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+
+    assert_response :no_content
+    assert_not @board.reload.published?
+  end
+
+  test "republishing after unpublishing issues a new key" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board)
+    old_key = @board.reload.publication.key
+    delete board_publication_path(@board)
+
+    post board_publication_path(@board)
+
+    assert_not_equal old_key, @board.reload.publication.key
+  end
+
+  test "publishing refreshes the cached board JSON" do
+    with_json_fragment_caching do
+      get board_path(@board), as: :json
+      assert_nil @response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+
+      post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+      assert_equal public_board_url(@board.reload.publication), @response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+
+      get board_path(@board), as: :json
+      assert_equal public_board_url(@board.publication), @response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+
+      delete board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+      get board_path(@board), as: :json
+      assert_nil @response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "non-admin cannot publish" do
+    logout_and_sign_in_as :jz
+
+    assert_no_difference -> { Board::Publication.count } do
+      post board_publication_path(@board)
+    end
+
+    assert_response :forbidden
+  end
+
+  test "non-admin cannot unpublish" do
+    @board.publish
+    logout_and_sign_in_as :jz
+
+    assert_no_difference -> { Board::Publication.count } do
+      delete board_publication_path(@board)
+    end
+
+    assert_response :forbidden
+    assert @board.reload.published?
+  end
+
+  test "board creator who is not an admin cannot publish" do
+    board = boards(:private)
+    board.update! creator: users(:jz)
+    board.accesses.revise granted: [ users(:jz) ], revoked: []
+    logout_and_sign_in_as :jz
+
+    post board_publication_path(board)
+
+    assert_response :forbidden
+    assert_not board.reload.published?
+  end
+
+  test "cannot publish a board the user has no access to" do
+    logout_and_sign_in_as :david
+    board = boards(:private)
+
+    post board_publication_path(board)
+
+    assert_response :not_found
+    assert_not board.reload.published?
+  end
+end
